{number: 161}
{title: Heaven Came Down}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O what a [F] wonderful, wonderful day,
Day I will never for-[C7] get;
After I'd wandered in darkness away,
Jesus my Savior I [F] met.
O what a tender, compassionate friend!
He met the [F7] need of my [Bb] heart;
Shadows dis-[F] pelling, with joy I am telling,
He [C7] made all the darkness de-[F] part!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F] Heaven came down and glory filled my soul,
When at the [C7] cross the Savior made me whole;
My sins were [F] washed away and my [Bb] night was turned to day,
[F] Heaven came down and [C7] glory filled my [F] soul!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Born [F] of the Spirit with life from above
Into God's fam'ly di-[C7] vine,
Justified fully thro' Calvary's love,
O what a standing is [F] mine!
And the trans-[F7] action so quickly was [Bb] made
When as a [F] sinner I came,
Took of the [C7] offer of grace He did proffer,
He [C7] saved me, O praise His dear [F] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Now [F] I've a hope that will surely endure
After the passing of [C7] time;
I have a future in heaven for sure,
There in those mansions sub-[F] lime.
And it's be-[F7] cause of that wonderful [Bb] day
When at the [F] cross I believed;
Riches e-[C7] ternal and blessings supernal
From [C7] His precious hand I re-[F] ceived.
{end_of_verse}
